{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42652751 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42652751 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42652751","source":"MED","pmid":"42652751","pmcid":"PMC13513615","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13513615"]},"doi":"10.3390/jcm15166347","title":"Psychological Factors to Consider in Treating Patients with Acne Vulgaris.","authorString":"Woźna J, Pazdrowski P, Welc N, Płócienniczak A, Korecka K, Żaba R, Grzybowski A, Mojs E.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Woźna J","lastName":"Woźna","firstName":"Julia","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Dermatology and Venereology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 60-355 Poznań, Poland."},{"affiliation":"Doctoral School, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 61-701 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Pazdrowski P","lastName":"Pazdrowski","firstName":"Paweł","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-9288-6257"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Doctoral School, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 61-701 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Welc N","lastName":"Welc","firstName":"Natalia","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Dermatology and Venereology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 60-355 Poznań, Poland."},{"affiliation":"Doctoral School, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 61-701 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Płócienniczak A","lastName":"Płócienniczak","firstName":"Anita","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Faculty of Medicine for Ms Anita Płócienniczak, Poznań University of Medical Sciences, 61-701 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Korecka K","lastName":"Korecka","firstName":"Katarzyna","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9473-1239"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Dermatology and Venereology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 60-355 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Żaba R","lastName":"Żaba","firstName":"Ryszard","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Dermatology and Venereology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 60-355 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Grzybowski A","lastName":"Grzybowski","firstName":"Andrzej","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3724-2391"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Ophthalmology, University of Warmia and Mazury, 10-719 Olsztyn, Poland."},{"affiliation":"Institute for Research in Ophthalmology, Foundation for Ophthalmology Development, 61-553 Poznań, Poland."}]}},{"fullName":"Mojs E","lastName":"Mojs","firstName":"Ewa","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Clinical Psychology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 61-701 Poznań, Poland."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3724-2391"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9473-1239"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-9288-6257"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"16","volume":"15","journalIssueId":4250095,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Clin Med","title":"Journal of clinical medicine","essn":"2077-0383","issn":"2077-0383","nlmid":"101606588","isoabbreviation":"J Clin Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-08-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"6347","abstractText":"Acne vulgaris is a chronic inflammatory skin disease associated with a substantial psychological burden that may extend beyond visible lesions and objective disease severity. Psychological factors such as stress, coping strategies, quality-of-life impairment, self-esteem, psychiatric symptoms, and treatment adherence are associated with disease perception, self-reported exacerbation, and treatment-related outcomes. This narrative review examines psychological stress and proposed biological mechanisms, coping strategies, treatment adherence, quality of life, self-esteem, sleep disturbance, and psychiatric comorbidity in people with acne. Relevant literature was identified through MEDLINE/PubMed, Scopus, Web of Science, and PsycINFO; the final literature search was conducted on 29 May 2026. Acne-specific studies were prioritized, with broader psychodermatology evidence used where acne-specific data were limited. The psychosocial burden of acne is individualized and only partly aligned with clinician-rated severity, supporting person-centered assessment. For each domain, the review outlines brief, commonly used screening instruments that may be feasible in routine dermatology. Incorporating psychological assessment and targeted supportive strategies into acne care may contribute to quality of life, adherence to therapy, and patient-centered care. The evidence is predominantly cross-sectional and derives from heterogeneous populations, instruments, and study designs, limiting causal inference.","affiliation":"Department of Dermatology and Venereology, Poznan University of Medical Sciences, 60-355 Poznań, Poland.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Quality of life","Acne vulgaris","Psychological stress","Treatment Adherence","Psychodermatology"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm15166347"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13513615"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13513615?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-08-27","dateOfCreation":"2026-08-27","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-29","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-08-17","firstPublicationDate":"2026-08-17","firstIndexDate":"2026-08-30","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-10","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}